From 017b8aae5baf1f764e127176a3c6e4d20b3c3ba3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:59:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Transaction closure: real portal execution,
 SessionVault/USDC signed paths, opt-in signing policy, fee audit

Source, research captures and offline tests only (no signing outside local test
chains, no sending, no wallet, no live change).
- L1: the PRODUCTION Base OptimismPortal 6.0.1 bytecode and the storage its
  deposit path reads (one public provider, block 0x1909a37; research
  provenance, captures refuse any failed read) executed on a local L1; the
  synthetic TransactionDeposited fixture is gone; checkPortalPin; matchDeposit
  verifier label is a parameter (anvil is labelled test-anvil-l1).
- src/vault-deposit.mjs: SessionVault owner-signed ops, session-key execute /
  terminateBySession, USDC EIP-3009 topUpWithAuthorization and the live
  ledger fundWithAuthorization, against the compiled production vault source;
  refuses an owner-equal deposit sender (the vault skips the opNonce for
  msg.sender == owner: shown double-executing on the real vault).
- src/lease-signing-policy.mjs: shared opt-in forced-inclusion lease signing
  (relay route unchanged at 300 s; forced route bounded, budgeted, refuses the
  production renewWindow instead of changing it, reports no continuity).
- fee audit with Base's production GasPriceOracle: the existing reserve pays a
  deposit lease ~3e9 wei against ~8.3e14 wei of L1 cost.
- NOTE-FOR-P-L1-BROADCAST.md: requirements for P's L1 pair (file note only).
